            <ArticleTitle>Transesophageal echocardiographic diagnosis of an aneurysm and thrombosis of the left anterior descending coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>655-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An aneurysm of the left anterior descending coronary artery with thrombosis in its lumen in a 36-year-old woman who had an acute myocardial infarction is described. Although the aneurysm was detected by angiography, a transesophageal study provided new specific details of the exact site of origin of the aneurysm, as well as vascular thrombosis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
